<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karlstad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karlstad is a city in Värmland in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, on the delta of the river Klarälven where it enters <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-vanern">Lake Vänern</a>. It received its town charter from Charles IX in 1584 and is named after him. In 1905 negotiations at Karlstad between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and Sweden produced the agreements under which Sweden accepted the peaceful dissolution of the union between the two kingdoms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karlstad.jpg" alt="Karlstad" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Visit Karlstad · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Areal_photo_of_Karlstad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
